From 1eb81c471f2c106f591ae48c33975053f362c732 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lech Piekarski <isilweo@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:38:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/34] media: venus: vdec: resume the core before a decoder
 command

After about 2 s without buffers runtime PM has cut the vcodec clocks.
Sending EOS (V4L2_DEC_CMD_STOP) to the firmware in that state hangs the
whole SoC on MSM8953; the board then resets through the secure watchdog
about 45 s later. This happens whenever an RTP stream feeding the decoder
stops and the pipeline is shut down with EOS.

Take a runtime PM reference around the decoder command.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c
index 530292c..7e1ecdb 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/vdec.c
@@ -545,6 +545,8 @@ static int vdec_subscribe_event(struct v4l2_fh *fh,
 	}
 }
 
+static int vdec_pm_get_put(struct venus_inst *inst);
+
 static int
 vdec_decoder_cmd(struct file *file, void *fh, struct v4l2_decoder_cmd *cmd)
 {
@@ -557,6 +559,11 @@ vdec_decoder_cmd(struct file *file, void *fh, struct v4l2_decoder_cmd *cmd)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/* sending a command with the vcodec clocks off hangs the SoC */
+	ret = vdec_pm_get_put(inst);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	mutex_lock(&inst->lock);
 
 	if (cmd->cmd == V4L2_DEC_CMD_STOP) {
